#####################################################################
# cp30_brick_cylinder.lgi
#
# group    : brick
# expect   : valid
# spec     : brick rtz 5,17,5 0.,0.,0. 2.,360.,2. 1,1,1
# points   : out_cp30_pts.inp
# mesh     : out_cp30_mesh.inp hex
# filter   : yes
#
# WHAT:
#   a hex cylinder (as the doc's example, smaller): radii 0, 0.5 ... 2;
#   angles 0, 22.5, ... 360; z = 0, 0.5, ... 2. The 0 / 360 deg seam and
#   the axis are vertices at the same place, so the brick is NOT closed
#   there: filter / rmpoint / compress / resetpts / itp (user, Oct 13)
#   merge them. The result is one connected mesh with valid topology;
#   the 64 hexes on the axis then list the axis vertices twice (their
#   axis face has area 0): reported as degenerate_cells (user, Oct 13).
# FROM THE DOCUMENTATION: CRTPTBRICK.md, last example
#####################################################################
cmo / create / mo_hex / / / hex
createpts / brick / rtz / 5,17,5 / 0.,0.,0. / 2.,360.,2. / 1,1,1
dump / avs / out_cp30_pts.inp / mo_hex
filter / 1,0,0
rmpoint / compress
resetpts / itp
quality
dump / avs / out_cp30_mesh.inp / mo_hex
finish
